{"response":"The Inference Engine is a really cool project where Drew serves local AI models right from his own hardware!

It runs on a **Framework Desktop's AMD APU**, which is notable because Drew had to hand-patch `llama.cpp` to get it working efficiently on hardware that isn't officially supported. He even fixed a GPU memory-allocator bug and found a 5x prefill speedup!

For software, it uses **`llama.cpp`** as the core inference engine, leveraging **ROCm** and **HIP** for GPU acceleration. It also integrates with **LiteLLM** for model routing and **Langfuse** for tracing agentic workflows. He's even set it up to be reachable remotely over **Telegram** for agentic workflows. [ACTIONS: view_projects]"}
